# PERFORMANCE RULES

Use:
- SARGable predicates;
- parameterized SQL;
- explicit joins;
- explicit column lists;
- set-based operations;
- appropriate pagination.

Avoid:
- SELECT *;
- implicit conversions;
- accidental Cartesian joins;
- unbounded result sets;
- N+1 patterns;
- unnecessary DISTINCT;
- unnecessary long transactions;
- NOLOCK as a generic fix.

Evidence required for important optimization:
- actual execution plan;
- CPU;
- logical reads;
- duration;
- representative row counts.

Never trade correctness/security for speed.
